# Copy to .env — Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time.
# With everything unset, the app runs fully local (stub channel, local
# anonymous identity, simulated room) — no backend needed for UI work.

# ---- Apple Music (MusicKit) ------------------------------------------
# Developer token (ES256 JWT signed with your MusicKit private key).
# Unlocks full-catalog synced playback for Apple Music subscribers.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APPLE_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=

# ---- Firebase ---------------------------------------------------------
# The `top-of-the-slops` web config ships as committed defaults in
# src/firebase.ts (client config is public by design). Override any value
# here per-environment; the one you're most likely to need is the RTDB
# URL if the database is created outside the default US region:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=

# Flip the LIVE room (RTDB channel + Firestore chat + presence + votes)
# once the conductor is deployed and writing /channels/global/state.
# Until then the stub room keeps everything runnable.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_CHANNEL=1

# ---- Conductor (server/conductor — set in Cloud Run, not here) -------
# FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://<project>-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com
# APPLE_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=            # catalog metadata for pool hydration
# POOL_SEARCH_TERM=synthwave        # dev-only pool seeding without a token
# VOTES_ENABLED=1                   # M4 switch: boo-to-skip + hype-to-replay
